  "summary": "An Oakland woman was pulled over by Alameda County sheriff's deputies after a Flock ALPR flagged her car, because thieves had swapped her license plates with ones tied to a serious crime. The article uses the incident to explore how plate-swapping is undermining the region's growing ALPR network and how data-hygiene failures can lead to wrongful stops.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "That is when it sort of hit me that I was being treated as a potential criminal and could have been hurt",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's a tactic that's been going on for a long time, but I think it's coming more into light now that we have these license plate readers",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "They are chasing license plates instead of criminals.",
      "paragraph_idx": 32
    }
  ],
